== exact in-degree variance and E[n(x)] for additive walks (all S enumerated) ==
N=7 nS=2 steps=(1, 2): E[Var indeg]=0.50000 E[n(x)]=0.50000  (nS-1)/nS=0.50000  nS/(nS-1)=2.00000
N=7 nS=3 steps=(1, 2, 4): E[Var indeg]=0.66667 E[n(x)]=0.66667  (nS-1)/nS=0.66667  nS/(nS-1)=1.50000
N=8 nS=4 steps=(1, 3, 5, 6): E[Var indeg]=0.75000 E[n(x)]=0.75000  (nS-1)/nS=0.75000  nS/(nS-1)=1.33333
N=9 nS=3 steps=(1, 2, 4): E[Var indeg]=0.66667 E[n(x)]=0.66667  (nS-1)/nS=0.66667  nS/(nS-1)=1.50000
  (population variance; Binomial(nS,1/nS) has Var=(nS-1)/nS; for a uniformly random map Var->1)

